From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:56:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 54/62] serve: STRATA_PREFIX_DIAG=1 logs where a long prompt
 read parted from recent prompts (opt-in, no content)

Long prompts read from 0 stall every slot, and the engine cannot say why nothing matched. With the env, the server
keeps a keyed block/token fingerprint of the last 64 requests (no token ids) and, for each read of at least
STRATA_PREFIX_DIAG_MIN tokens (8192), prints the longest shared start with any of them, which one, where it ran and
where in the chat template the two part (system message, tool list, tool response, thinking...), never the text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
